# Design System Rule

## Core Principles
- Use semantic tokens from `frontend/app/globals.css`; do not hardcode one-off colors unless there is no matching token.
- Favor reusable primitives from `frontend/components/ui/*` and layout primitives from `frontend/components/layout/*`.
- Keep visual hierarchy intentional: display typography for large section headlines, Inter for UI/body, JetBrains Mono for compact labels.

## Token Usage
- Colors: use `background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `accent`, `accent-secondary`, `border`, `ring`, `card`.
- Effects: use shared radius and shadow scales; avoid introducing ad hoc radii and custom drop shadows.
- Prefer gradient signature (`accent` to `accent-secondary`) for primary emphasis only.

## Component Consistency
- Reuse `Button`, `Card`, `Badge`, and `Input` variants before introducing bespoke class strings.
- Keep controls accessible: visible focus ring, 44px+ targets, readable contrast.
- Avoid nested card shells for page sections; reserve cards for repeated items or framed tool areas.

## Responsiveness
- Maintain stable layout dimensions at all breakpoints.
- Preserve section rhythm through tokenized spacing and container constraints.
